{
    "background_story": "Kiya was a brilliant and reclusive puppeteer who brought her creations to life with an uncanny magic. Growing up in a family of skilled artisans, she learned the art of puppetry from a young age. Kiya's puppets were more than just wooden dolls on strings; they were vessels for the stories and emotions she wanted to convey. Her most famous creation, a puppet named Luna, was said to have a mind of its own. Kiya's fingers danced across the strings, imbuing Luna with a depth and nuance that mesmerized audiences worldwide. As Kiya's fame grew, so did the mystique surrounding her puppets. People whispered that she was a master manipulator, not just of strings, but of the very fabric of reality. Kiya's puppets became a reflection of her own inner world, a world where the lines between reality and fantasy blurred.",
